IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Act, section 2 (Interpretation): the payment period, the payment quarter, the first and
-- second adjustment quarters, and the Consumer Price Index for an adjustment quarter.
--
-- Each rule is given a DATE and works on the month that contains it (a month is the DATE of its first day;
-- see oas-core). The answers are Calendar spans. Every month has exactly one payment period and one payment
-- quarter, so these rules are total.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "payment period, in relation to a month"
--
-- FORK F2 (NOTES.md): paragraph (a) says "the fiscal year that includes the month" and the Act does not
-- say when a fiscal year begins. It is taken to begin in April: paragraph (b) starts the next period on
-- April 1, 1998, immediately after a fiscal year that ended on March 31, 1998. That is an inference from
-- the text, not a statement in it, so it is a named value that a reviewer can find and change.
-- src:60 | (b) the period that begins on April 1, 1998 and ends on June 30, 1999, where that period includes the month, and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "payment period", paragraph (b) (src:60)
`the month in which a fiscal year begins` MEANS 4

-- "payment period, in relation to a month, means (a) the fiscal year that includes the month, where the month is
-- before April, 1998, (b) ... and (c) ..." (all three paragraphs are quoted here)
-- src:58 | payment period, in relation to a month, means
-- src:59 | (a) the fiscal year that includes the month, where the month is before April, 1998,
-- src:60 | (b) the period that begins on April 1, 1998 and ends on June 30, 1999, where that period includes the month, and
-- src:61 | (c) the period after June 30, 1999 that begins on July 1 of one year and ends on June 30 of the next year, where that period includes the month; (période de paiement)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "payment period" (src:58-61)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Calendar span`
`the payment period in relation to the month containing` d MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- (a) the fiscal year that includes the month, where the month is before April, 1998
        IF month LESS THAN (YearMonthDay 1998 4 1)
        THEN `Calendar span` WITH
                 `first day` IS YearMonthDay fiscalYear (`the month in which a fiscal year begins`) 1
                 `last day`  IS (YearMonthDay (fiscalYear PLUS 1) (`the month in which a fiscal year begins`) 1) MINUS 1
        -- (b) the period that begins on April 1, 1998 and ends on June 30, 1999, where that period includes the month
        IF month LESS THAN (YearMonthDay 1999 7 1)
        THEN `Calendar span` WITH
                 `first day` IS YearMonthDay 1998 4 1
                 `last day`  IS YearMonthDay 1999 6 30
        -- (c) the period after June 30, 1999 that begins on July 1 of one year and ends on June 30 of the next year
        OTHERWISE
            `Calendar span` WITH
                 `first day` IS YearMonthDay julyYear 7 1
                 `last day`  IS YearMonthDay (julyYear PLUS 1) 6 30
    WHERE
        month MEANS `the first day of the month containing` d
        fiscalYear MEANS
            IF DATE_MONTH month AT LEAST (`the month in which a fiscal year begins`)
            THEN DATE_YEAR month
            ELSE DATE_YEAR month MINUS 1
        julyYear MEANS
            IF DATE_MONTH month AT LEAST 7
            THEN DATE_YEAR month
            ELSE DATE_YEAR month MINUS 1

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "payment quarter means a period of three months commencing on the first day of April, July, October
-- or January in a payment period"
-- src:62 | payment quarter means a period of three months commencing on the first day of April, July, October or January in a payment period; (trimestre de paiement)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "payment quarter" (src:62)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Calendar span`
`the payment quarter containing the month containing` d MEANS
    `Calendar span` WITH
        `first day` IS first
        `last day`  IS `the last day of the month containing` (`add months` first 2)
    WHERE
        -- January, April, July or October: the first month of the calendar quarter that holds d
        first MEANS Date 1 ((FLOOR ((DATE_MONTH d MINUS 1) DIVIDED BY 3) TIMES 3) PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR d)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "first adjustment quarter, in relation to a payment quarter": the three months that begin 5 months
-- before the payment quarter, written out as the four paragraphs of the definition.
-- The input is any date in the payment quarter.
-- src:24 | first adjustment quarter, in relation to a payment quarter, means,
-- src:25 | (a) if the payment quarter commences on the first day of April in a payment period, the period of three months commencing on the first day of November immediately before that first day of April,
-- src:26 | (b) if the payment quarter commences on the first day of July in a payment period, the period of three months commencing on the first day of February immediately before that first day of July,
-- src:27 | (c) if the payment quarter commences on the first day of October in a payment period, the period of three months commencing on the first day of May immediately before that first day of October, and
-- src:28 | (d) if the payment quarter commences on the first day of January in a payment period, the period of three months commencing on the first day of August immediately before that first day of January; (premier trimestre de rajustement)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "first adjustment quarter" (src:24-28)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Calendar span`
`the first adjustment quarter in relation to the payment quarter containing` d MEANS
    `Calendar span` WITH
        `first day` IS start
        `last day`  IS `the last day of the month containing` (`add months` start 2)
    WHERE
        quarter MEANS `the payment quarter containing the month containing` d
        quarterYear MEANS DATE_YEAR (quarter's `first day`)
        start MEANS
            BRANCH
                -- (a) the payment quarter commences on the first day of April: the three months commencing on the first day of November immediately before
                IF DATE_MONTH (quarter's `first day`) EQUALS 4
                THEN YearMonthDay (quarterYear MINUS 1) 11 1
                -- (b) July: the three months commencing on the first day of February immediately before
                IF DATE_MONTH (quarter's `first day`) EQUALS 7
                THEN YearMonthDay quarterYear 2 1
                -- (c) October: the three months commencing on the first day of May immediately before
                IF DATE_MONTH (quarter's `first day`) EQUALS 10
                THEN YearMonthDay quarterYear 5 1
                -- (d) January: the three months commencing on the first day of August immediately before
                OTHERWISE YearMonthDay (quarterYear MINUS 1) 8 1

-- "second adjustment quarter, in relation to a payment quarter": the three months that begin 8 months
-- before the payment quarter, written out as the four paragraphs of the definition.
-- src:68 | second adjustment quarter, in relation to a payment quarter, means,
-- src:69 | (a) if the payment quarter commences on the first day of April in a payment period, the period of three months commencing on the first day of August immediately before that first day of April,
-- src:70 | (b) if the payment quarter commences on the first day of July in a payment period, the period of three months commencing on the first day of November immediately before that first day of July,
-- src:71 | (c) if the payment quarter commences on the first day of October in a payment period, the period of three months commencing on the first day of February immediately before that first day of October, and
-- src:72 | (d) if the payment quarter commences on the first day of January in a payment period, the period of three months commencing on the first day of May immediately before that first day of January; (second trimestre de rajustement)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "second adjustment quarter" (src:68-72)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Calendar span`
`the second adjustment quarter in relation to the payment quarter containing` d MEANS
    `Calendar span` WITH
        `first day` IS start
        `last day`  IS `the last day of the month containing` (`add months` start 2)
    WHERE
        quarter MEANS `the payment quarter containing the month containing` d
        quarterYear MEANS DATE_YEAR (quarter's `first day`)
        start MEANS
            BRANCH
                -- (a) April: the three months commencing on the first day of August immediately before
                IF DATE_MONTH (quarter's `first day`) EQUALS 4
                THEN YearMonthDay (quarterYear MINUS 1) 8 1
                -- (b) July: the three months commencing on the first day of November immediately before
                IF DATE_MONTH (quarter's `first day`) EQUALS 7
                THEN YearMonthDay (quarterYear MINUS 1) 11 1
                -- (c) October: the three months commencing on the first day of February immediately before
                IF DATE_MONTH (quarter's `first day`) EQUALS 10
                THEN YearMonthDay quarterYear 2 1
                -- (d) January: the three months commencing on the first day of May immediately before
                OTHERWISE YearMonthDay (quarterYear MINUS 1) 5 1

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "Consumer Price Index, with respect to any adjustment quarter, means the average for that adjustment
-- quarter of the Consumer Price Index for Canada, as published by Statistics Canada ..., for each month in
-- that adjustment quarter". An adjustment quarter has three months, so the three published monthly figures
-- are the inputs. The average is not rounded here: Regulations s 9(1) and (2) say how the average is
-- determined and expressed (to one decimal place, `rounded half up to the number of decimal places`), and
-- that is encoded by piece oa3; a rule that needs the figure in the form the Regulations give calls
-- oa3's rule on the result of this one.
-- src:23 | Consumer Price Index, with respect to any adjustment quarter, means the average for that adjustment quarter of the Consumer Price Index for Canada, as published by Statistics Canada under the authority of the Statistics Act, for each month in that adjustment quarter; (indice des prix à la consommation)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "Consumer Price Index" (src:23)
GIVEN `figure for the first month`  IS A NUMBER
      `figure for the second month` IS A NUMBER
      `figure for the third month`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Consumer Price Index for an adjustment quarter` `figure for the first month` `figure for the second month` `figure for the third month` MEANS
    (`figure for the first month` PLUS `figure for the second month` PLUS `figure for the third month`) DIVIDED BY 3
